{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":26270834,"ns":0,"title":"Consensus dynamics","extract":"Consensus dynamics, also known as agreement dynamics, is an area of research at the intersection of systems theory and graph theory. It studies how a group of agents—such as robots, sensors, or decision-makers—interacting over a network can reach a common decision or estimate through local rules and information exchange.","description":"How a group of agents can reach a common decision","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}